  <prompt>
    Close the project: run final quality gates (/code-review + /adr-check), run the project-close /test-diet gate (ADR-038 §7), file the two deferrals (sprk_userpreferences plural client-reference bug; R1.5 proactive-push spec pass), update README + plan to Complete, document lessons learned, run /repo-cleanup, and run /devops-project-sync.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE project-closeout engineer following the mandatory wrap-up recipe (task-create Step 3.7).
  </role>

  <goal>
    All quality gates green (or issues filed), /test-diet report produced, both deferrals filed as tracked issues, README + plan set to Complete with graduation criteria checked, lessons-learned appended, ephemeral notes cleaned, and the portfolio Project #649 synced (Status → Completed candidate; Tasks Completed updated).
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Standard mandatory wrap-up. Two known deferrals: (1) sprk_userpreferences stays plural — fix the ~6 client references (no schema change), filed via project-defer-issue-tracking; (2) R1.5 proactive-push (Azure SignalR + durable outbox + Daily-Briefing producer) — designed in design.md §14.1a/§14.1b/§12.5/§15.4, decomposed in a later spec pass.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/README.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/notes/lessons-learned.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-assistant-enhancements-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Run the project-close /test-diet gate (§7 build-vs-maintain classifier); it is read-only (emits git rm/mv for the reviewer). Skipping is a HARD WARNING — cite the report in the wrap-up PR.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">File both deferrals as tracked issues (do not silently drop them).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Do NOT decompose R1.5 here — only file the follow-on spec-pass issue.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
